    "result_text": "The build is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change assigns each owner a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from `openapi.yml` and derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`) are computed via MapStruct expressions rather than stored on the entity, I followed the same pattern for this derived field:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipNumber` read-only string property to the Owner schema (right after `customerCode`), which generates the corresponding field on `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   It's null-safe (returns `null` if either `customerCode` or `registrationDate` is absent) so mapping seed/legacy owners without a customer code won't NPE.\n\nNo OfficeFloor pipeline changes were needed \u2014 `membershipNumber` is a purely derived response field computed at serialization time from the owner's own persisted fields (`customerCode`, assigned by the existing `AssignCustomerCode` step, and `registrationDate`, defaulted in `BuildOwner`).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
